Do not force -pie for shared libraries.

CMake appends the global link option -pie after -shared on the linker command
line.  GCC 16 then links the executable startup object Scrt1.o into
libdeepin-pdfium-reader.so, and the link fails with "undefined reference to
`main'".  PIE is the default of the Arch toolchain, so the option is redundant.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -255,4 +255,3 @@
 add_link_options(
-    -pie
     -z lazy
 )
